    <!-- Chosen Palette: Warm Neutrals with Subtle Blue/Green Accents -->
    <!-- Application Structure Plan: A user-centric dashboard design. The initial view presents top-level insights: key stats, best bets, and top jockey/trainer charts. This provides immediate, actionable information. The core of the app is an interactive "Race Explorer" where the user selects a race from a dropdown to dynamically load detailed analysis for that specific race. This prevents overwhelming the user with all 10 races at once and mimics a handicapper's workflow of focusing on one race at a time. This structure is chosen for usability and efficient information retrieval over a simple linear report. -->
    <!-- Visualization & Content Choices: Report Info -> Goal -> Viz/Presentation Method -> Interaction -> Justification -> Library/Method. | Jockey/Trainer Stats -> Compare -> Bar/Donut Charts -> Hover -> Best for comparing categories/proportions -> Chart.js/Canvas. | Best Bets -> Inform -> Styled Cards -> None -> Highlights key takeaways -> HTML/Tailwind. | Race-by-Race Data -> Organize/Inform -> Dropdown-driven content -> Select race -> Focused analysis, prevents overload -> Vanilla JS. | Top Speed Figures -> Compare -> Horizontal Bar Chart -> Hover -> Good for many categories & long labels -> Chart.js/Canvas. | Pace Logic -> Organize -> Flowchart Diagram -> None -> Visual explanation is intuitive -> HTML/Tailwind. | CONFIRMING NO SVG/Mermaid. -->
    <!-- CONFIRMATION: NO SVG graphics used. NO Mermaid JS used. -->
